/* =====================================================================
   MOST LIKELY: character traits. How each character actually behaves in canon (anime + manga), scored 0-9 per trait.
   The personality duels ("Who is kinder?", "Who would betray their friends first?") are built from these scores, so a
   character is judged the same way on every board and in every duel, and two characters are only duelled when their
   scores differ by at least two points (a clear difference, never a coin flip).

   Scale: 9 = a defining trait, shown again and again; 7-8 strong; 5-6 moderate or only in some situations; 3-4 weak;
          0-2 the opposite is what the story shows. A character is scored ONLY on traits the story clearly shows;
          a missing trait means "not shown either way", and the character simply isn't on that board.
   Rules: behaviour on screen, not reputation, popularity or fan jokes; the whole story, not one arc (how much a
          character changes is its own trait, X); a cold-acting character can still be kind; battle cleverness is
          not honesty or maturity; being quiet is not the same as keeping secrets.
   These are the editors' reading of the story, not official data: the board label says so, and tools/feud-check.mjs
   enforces the ANCHORS below (facts of the story every score has to agree with) and flags contradictory pairs.
   ===================================================================== */
